{"id": "EUVD-2026-101740", "enisaUuid": "7a3941ee-ca12-3708-8393-91dae66f2efd", "description": "GitPython before 3.2.0 contains a remote code execution vulnerability that allows attackers to run commands because Git.ls_remote forwards URLs without check_unsafe_protocols validation. Attackers can supply ext:: remote-helper URLs to execute commands when git permits the ext transport, while merge_base and IndexFile.move also accept unguarded option injection.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T13:36:14", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/security/advisories/GHSA-w8jc-g24h-crhw", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitpython-before-3.2.0-command-execution-via-ls-remote-ext-urls"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jj45-mj3g-556c", "CVE-2026-110857"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "dbf3c98a-29bf-3503-a0ef-de4c6147e058", "product": {"name": "GitPython", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5d6f7fb1-23e8-3174-a4fd-7045e580c4bf", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}], "isExploited": false}